# Memcheck suppressions for the Rust core (ci.yml's valgrind lanes).
#
# Rust's hashbrown keeps a pointer into the middle of its allocation (the
# control bytes that follow the buckets), not to its start. A HashMap still
# alive at exit, such as the table of operations in flight in the file-I/O
# proactor the engine keeps for the whole process, is therefore reported as
# "possibly lost" although it is reachable. Only that kind, and only
# allocations made by hashbrown's tables, is suppressed.
{
   rust-hashbrown-table-reachable-through-interior-pointer
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:*hashbrown*RawTable*
}
{
   rust-hashbrown-table-reachable-through-interior-pointer-realloc
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:realloc
   ...
   fun:*hashbrown*RawTable*
}
